-- Refs #182 (pool data inconsistencies, part 1 of 4: pool_template rows for the per-map pieces)
-- ERROR CLASS: `pool_gameobject`/`pool_creature` has spawns on multiple different maps ... skipped (PoolMgr.cpp:536,614) and
--   `pool_pool` has child pools on multiple maps (PoolMgr.cpp:709). A pool has ONE map (PoolTemplateData::MapId, set by the
--   first loaded member); every later member on another map is dropped, and because ObjectMgr only grid-spawns gameobjects/creatures
--   that are NOT in a pool (ObjectMgr.cpp:2132,2492), each dropped member NEVER spawns (a gathering-node / creature gap).
-- FIX (this file + _41, _42, _43): split every mixed-map pool into one pool per map. The original pool id keeps the map of its first
--   loaded member (the map the core already chose, so what works today is unchanged); each other map gets a NEW pool id
--   1000000 + old_id*8 + n (n = 1..3, ascending map id; the largest old id is 30184 so the range is far from existing ids)
--   with the same max_limit and the description "<old description> [map M, split of pool OLD]".
--   2335 pools are mixed-map (1738 members-only pools + 597 mother pools); 2534 new pieces. MoP 5.4.8 carries the same rows
--   (pool_template/pool_gameobject/pool_pool), i.e. it is inherited data, not an LoA regression.
-- This file only inserts the 2534 piece templates (INSERT IGNORE: re-runnable). _41/_42 move the members, _43 re-links mother pools.
-- Apply _40.._43 together: until the members are moved the new pools are empty ("Pool Id N is empty" lines).
-- VERIFY:  SELECT COUNT(*) FROM pool_template WHERE entry >= 1000000;   -- 2534 after apply
-- UNDO:    DELETE FROM pool_template WHERE entry >= 1000000;  (after undoing _41/_42/_43)
